  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d71e962d6af69bf4f8e4449472844fc2, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My evening census route! District eleven, blocks four through nine. Every door answered but two. I reported which two. That was the best part.
    midDaysAnswer: The district office. I brought corrections to the registry, and the names of everyone who questioned the curfew. They thanked me. By name.
    finalDaysAnswer: The last addresses on my list. The doors were open, as instructed. I recorded what I found inside. Obedient to the end. I was so proud of them.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The tram depot. I work the ticket office there. The census forms are only something I help with on Sundays.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The district office. I had to explain why the registry is late. I have been careless with it lately. It happens.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: From the western district. I only moved to this town last month, so I do not know this crossing well.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No! I report my own health to the district office every morning, as instructed. It is my favourite part of the day.
    midDaysAnswer: I sleep less since the blast. Three hours, perhaps four. Who could sleep? The State is doing so much. I listen to every broadcast.
    finalDaysAnswer: None. If I had any, the State would tell me. And if it does, I will thank it for noticing.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My eyes, a little. Faces blur together these days. I could not tell you who sat at this window before you.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. I sleep very well. My husband makes sure of it. He does not let me work at night.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Only forgetfulness. I lose names now. Yesterday I could not recall my own block number.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I have recorded every resident in this district. The State knows them all now. Is that not a comfort?
    - You are the fourth officer at this post. The third one asked what really happened the night of the blast. He was not here for long.
    - People say the State is cold. The State is a mother! And look how hard she is working for us.
    midDays:
    - The list is shorter than it was. Those people did not listen. It is all going exactly to plan.
    - Every window on my street broke inward the night of the blast. Not mine. I had taped them, as instructed. I was so proud.
    - I wrote your name down. Do not worry! It is a list of the faithful. For now.
    finalDays:
    - When the State arrives, it will save everyone on the list. I keep the list. I check it every night. It is so close now.
    - Whatever the blast was, it was permitted. That is what makes it beautiful. Nothing happens here without permission.
    - Doubt spreads faster than any sickness. I report both. Happily!
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 7070787
